Modeling changes of the MQT-TZ RA (hot_cache/host/main.c of mqttz/optee-apps, as published), applied
before tools/lang-preprocess.py preprocesses it.  The model keeps payload_reencryption, the call of
the TA; main.imp is the entry point of the model in place of main, parse_arguments and the
benchmark loop.

1. The TA runs on the memory of the RA (the shared memory of the spec), so the RA passes its
   clients as they are: params[0] is the origin client and params[1] the destination client, each
   a pointer to its mqttz_client.  Upstream copies the fields of a client into one buffer
   (id | iv | data), as "the internal structure is lost in the REE -> TEE communication", and the
   TA finds them by offsets; in the model a field of the struct is the part of the buffer at its
   offset.  The TA writes the result through dest->data.
2. The timing (params[2], parsed with strtok afterwards) and the benchmark values (params[3]:
   key_mode and first) are left out, as in the TA (model.patch of the TA, 1 and 5).  So are the
   session context (ctx: the session is passed as it is), the buffer sizes and the logging.
3. The return code.  TEEC_InvokeCommand returns TEE_ERROR_TARGET_DEAD when the TA panics, and else
   the return code of the TA.  The model has the two apart: the TA writes its code to its output
   parameter, which the model passes as the location of ta_res (see the [ra.host] table), and the
   call returns success or target-dead.  So res is the code of the TA after a successful call.

